---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { docsUrl } from '../lib/urls';
---
<Base
  title="404 — Dead Letter | Nexus"
  description="This message was undeliverable. No actor registered at this path."
>
  <section class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-24 text-center">
    <p class="text-7xl mb-6" aria-hidden="true">📭</p>
    <h2 class="text-4xl font-extrabold mb-4">404 — Dead Letter</h2>
    <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-4">
      In Nexus, a message sent to an actor that no longer exists (or never did) is
      routed to the <code class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">DeadLetterRef</code> —
      a null-object sink that captures undeliverable envelopes so they're never silently
      dropped. Every dead letter is logged.
    </p>
    <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-10">
      The URL you requested doesn't match any route on this site. It has been safely
      delivered to the dead-letter queue.
    </p>
    <a
      href="/"
      class="inline-block bg-primary hover:bg-primary-dark text-white px-8 py-3 rounded-md font-semibold transition"
    >
      Back to home
    </a>
    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
      Looking for the docs? They live at
      <a href={docsUrl()} class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-slate-700 dark:hover:text-slate-300">
        docs.nexusactors.com
      </a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
